<!-- VALUE CAPTURE -->
<section id="capture">
  <div class="section-inner">
    <div class="section-label">Theory of Value Capture</div>
    <div class="two-col fade-in">
      <div>
        <h2>Where the<br><em>Money Pools</em></h2>
        <p>History shows substrate alone rarely captures the lion's share. In PCs, Microsoft owned the OS while Intel built the chips. In mobile, Apple captured the integrated experience. In cloud, AWS owned the platform while server makers commoditised.</p>
        <p>In bio-compute, value pools at the control/firmware layer and the proprietary stimulus→outcome map — the dataset of (state, stimulus, context) → (response trajectory, outcome). This map compounds via network effects, switching costs, and regulatory capture.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>Cortical Labs and FinalSpark are substrate-heavy today. Their cloud rental models position them to own the map as users generate data. The winning architecture resembles NVIDIA crossed with AWS: hardware + CUDA plus rentable infrastructure + APIs.</p>
        <p><strong style="color:var(--text);">The critical question:</strong> who owns the data generated on the platform? This is not abstract — it is the entire moat question in one contractual clause.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="vc-row fade-in">
      <div class="vc-card">
        <div class="vc-layer">Layer 1</div>
        <div class="vc-title">Substrate</div>
        <div class="vc-desc">Organoids, iPSC lines, perfusion systems. Will commoditise as standardisation matures. Feeders to the platform above.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="vc-card">
        <div class="vc-layer">Layer 2</div>
        <div class="vc-title">I/O & Hardware</div>
        <div class="vc-desc">MEAs, Neuralink-style threads, stimulation channels. Rapid iteration. Chinese competition. Commodity within 5 years.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="vc-card active">
        <div class="vc-layer">Layer 3</div>
        <div class="vc-title">Control / Map</div>
        <div class="vc-desc">Proprietary stimulus→outcome dataset at scale. Validated protocols. Regulatory-grade submissions. Network effects. Switching costs. This is the moat.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="divider"></div>

<!-- WORKLOADS -->
<section style="background:var(--bg2);">
  <div class="section-inner">
    <div class="section-label">Killer Workloads</div>
    <h2 class="fade-in">Where Biology<br><em>Actually Wins</em></h2>
    <p class="fade-in" style="max-width:600px;">Biology is not general compute. It is the specialised layer for workloads where embodiment and native dynamics deliver unmatchable value. Name the workload. Name the win metric. Reject everything else.</p>

    <div class="workload-row fade-in">
      <div class="workload-item">
        <div>
          <div class="wl-type">Base Case</div>
          <div class="wl-title">Biology-Native Prediction</div>
          <div class="wl-metric">Drug screening · NAMs · Organoid assays</div>
        </div>
        <div class="wl-win">Predict human response, toxicity, and efficacy ranking under perturbations. The substrate <em>is</em> the human-relevant dynamics silicon can only simulate expensively. 90% of drugs passing preclinical testing fail in humans — bio-compute's edge is closing that gap.</div>
        <div class="wl-clock">No clock<br>constraint</div>
      </div>
      <div class="workload-item">
        <div>
          <div class="wl-type">Secondary</div>
          <div class="wl-title">Closed-Loop Adaptive Control</div>
          <div class="wl-metric">Robotics · Edge AI · Non-stationary environments</div>
        </div>
        <div class="wl-win">Stabilisation and adaptation under drift and shifting physical conditions. Win metric: joules per useful adaptation, sample efficiency, recovery after simulated damage.</div>
        <div class="wl-clock">ms–s tasks<br>only</div>
      </div>
      <div class="workload-item">
        <div>
          <div class="wl-type">Call Option</div>
          <div class="wl-title">Dynamics Coprocessor</div>
          <div class="wl-metric">Reservoir-style nonlinear tasks</div>
        </div>
        <div class="wl-win">Energy per prediction under drift vs analog/memristor silicon equivalents. Biology provides the reservoir for free.</div>
        <div class="wl-clock">2030+</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="metrics fade-in">
      <div class="metric"><span class="metric-val">~20W</span><div class="metric-lbl">Human brain power draw</div></div>
      <div class="metric"><span class="metric-val">~40MW</span><div class="metric-lbl">GPT-4 class training run</div></div>
      <div class="metric"><span class="metric-val">90%</span><div class="metric-lbl">Drugs failing after preclinical</div></div>
      <div class="metric"><span class="metric-val">4mm</span><div class="metric-lbl">Necrosis wall without vascularisation</div></div>
      <div class="metric"><span class="metric-val">2027</span><div class="metric-lbl">Transfer-function proof window</div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="divider"></div>

<!-- BOTTLENECKS -->
<section id="bottlenecks">
  <div class="section-inner">
    <div class="section-label">Investment Bottlenecks</div>
    <h2 class="fade-in">Ranked by<br><em>Lethality</em></h2>
    <p class="fade-in" style="max-width:640px;">No thesis survives contact with reality without ruthless mapping of failure modes. These are the structural bottlenecks, ranked in order of how likely each is to kill the investment case.</p>

    <div class="bottleneck-list fade-in">

      <div class="bn-item">
        <div class="bn-num">1</div>
        <div class="bn-body">
          <div class="bn-title">Programming & Knowledge Transfer</div>
          <div class="bn-desc">DishBrain showed learning is possible. Generalisation, reproducibility at scale, and persistence across replacements remain open. Fresh organoid may equal tabula rasa — this is potentially thesis-breaking. Acceptance test: time-to-task curve with variance across N units published by mid-2027.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="bn-badge badge-critical">Core Unsolved</div>
      </div>

      <div class="bn-item">
        <div class="bn-num">2</div>
        <div class="bn-body">
          <div class="bn-title">Agency & Goal Conflict</div>
          <div class="bn-desc">Cells optimise survival. Drift is native, not a bug. An organoid may optimise "stay alive" over your assigned task. Test: transfer-function stability (input X → output distribution Y) across 100+ units with reward-loop enforcement.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="bn-badge badge-critical">Existential</div>
      </div>

      <div class="bn-item">
        <div class="bn-num">3</div>
        <div class="bn-body">
          <div class="bn-title">Ops & Holding Costs</div>
          <div class="bn-desc">Tissue never sleeps. System-level energy (perfusion + MEA + compute overhead) must deliver clear advantage over silicon including idle-time. Target: 70%+ utilisation and low contamination/MTTR. Fully burdened $/wetware-hour is the number that matters.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="bn-badge badge-high">Economic</div>
      </div>

      <div class="bn-item">
        <div class="bn-num">4</div>
        <div class="bn-body">
          <div class="bn-title">Neuromorphic Silicon Competition</div>
          <div class="bn-desc">Intel Hala Point (1.15B neurons on Loihi 2) and IBM NorthPole deliver low-power continual learning deterministically — no necrosis, no ethics overhead, no idle cost. Biology's edge: true embodiment for human-relevant prediction. Head-to-head on defined metrics (joules/adaptation, robustness under drift) is required.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="bn-badge badge-high">Strategic</div>
      </div>

      <div class="bn-item">
        <div class="bn-num">5</div>
        <div class="bn-body">
          <div class="bn-title">Timescale Mismatch & 3D Scaling</div>
          <div class="bn-desc">Millisecond biology limits applications to real-world control and prediction. The necrosis wall (~4mm without vascularisation) caps organoid size. Perfusion and bioprinting roadmaps are the unlock — track Vivodyne-style vascular printing.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="bn-badge badge-high">Physical</div>
      </div>

      <div class="bn-item">
        <div class="bn-num">6</div>
        <div class="bn-body">
          <div class="bn-title">Ethics, Regulation & Moratorium Risk</div>
          <div class="bn-desc">Live tripwires: NHMRC National Statement 2025 (organoids, effective early 2026); EU 2024–25 in-vitro neurological model guidance; FDA 2025 NAMs acceleration. Levin's "cognition all the way down" is not philosophy — it is a direct challenge to the regulatory framework. Companies without early IRB engagement face existential compliance risk.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="bn-badge badge-med">Regulatory</div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="divider"></div>

<!-- 2030 SCENARIOS -->
<section id="2030" style="background:var(--bg2);">
  <div class="section-inner">
    <div class="section-label">2030 Scenarios</div>
    <h2 class="fade-in">What the World Looks Like<br><em>If This Works</em></h2>
    <p class="fade-in" style="max-width:640px;">In the success scenario, the AI infrastructure crisis has become the dominant constraint on technological progress. Power demand from data centres doubled 2025–2028. Hyperscalers are paying spot electricity prices that would have been unthinkable in 2020. Bio-compute has found its wedge.</p>

    <div class="scenario-grid fade-in">
      <div class="scenario-card bull">
        <span class="scenario-tag tag-bull">Bull Case · 2030</span>
        <div class="scenario-num">$2B</div>
        <div class="scenario-label">Cortical Labs valuation range · 8–12× ARR</div>
        <div class="scenario-items">
          <div class="scenario-item">$180–250M ARR. 60% large pharma, 25% CROs, 15% academic & government.</div>
          <div class="scenario-item">68% gross margin. Protocol licensing layer sitting above hardware drives premium.</div>
          <div class="scenario-item">4.2M validated assay endpoints across 340 compounds. No competitor has more than 800k.</div>
          <div class="scenario-item">GxP certification achieved 2027 after FDA NAMs engagement. Inside procurement of 11 top-20 pharma companies.</div>
          <div class="scenario-item">CL1 Gen 3: 14–18 month organoid lifespan. 8-minute AI-assisted calibration.</div>
          <div class="scenario-item">FinalSpark: $400–700M. AWS of wetware for research. Acquired by Thermo Fisher or Merck KGaA.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="scenario-card bear">
        <span class="scenario-tag tag-bear">Bear Case · 2030</span>
        <div class="scenario-num" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--muted),#444);-webkit-background-clip:text;-webkit-text-fill-color:transparent;">TBD</div>
        <div class="scenario-label">The programming problem remains unsolved</div>
        <div class="scenario-items">
          <div class="scenario-item">Transfer function variance never came below 35% across units. Pharma ran pilots, found results irreproducible, returned to established in vitro methods.</div>
          <div class="scenario-item">FinalSpark pivoted to pure research tools. Cortical Labs raised a down round in 2028.</div>
          <div class="scenario-item">Neuromorphic silicon (Hala Point, NorthPole) captured all edge AI workloads with deterministic results.</div>
          <div class="scenario-item">Bio-compute became a footnote in the 2030s synthetic biology hype cycle analysis.</div>
          <div class="scenario-item" style="border-left-color:var(--accent);color:rgba(232,232,240,0.8);">The tell is visible by mid-2027: cross-unit reproducibility data, published with variance, on a commercially relevant assay.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="pull-quote fade-in" style="border-color:var(--accent3);margin-top:64px;">
      "The data moat in bio-compute compounds fastest for first movers. The window to anchor the proprietary stimulus-outcome dataset before well-capitalised competitors enter is measured in months, not years."
    </div>
